# Code settings

Read `Agents/Settings/CONFIG.md` for **Test default**, **Enable edit**, **MEMORY.md path**, and **Memory max lines**.

Do not create, edit, or delete a file in this hub unless **Enable edit** is `true`. Missing or any other value means disabled. Read that field immediately before a hub edit. If editing is disabled, ask **Yes** / **No** to enable it. **No** stops and does not edit. **Yes** sets **Enable edit** to `true`, then makes the requested edit. Help → **Enable edit** may set the flag. This applies to every agent, in Cursor and Claude.

After a code or UI update, read **Test default** and do only that. `UNIT` runs unit tests. `BROWSER` checks the change in the browser. `BOTH` does both. `NONE` does neither: do not run unit tests and do not open the browser. A standing instruction to verify UI in the browser does not override `NONE`. Only that same prompt asking for a unit test or a browser test overrides it, and that does not change `CONFIG.md`. Missing or any other value skips tests. Read `Agents/Rules/code-settings/code-settings.md` when changing **Test default**. Do not open that file on any other prompt.

When the prompt is only `HELP` or `/help`, read and follow `Agents/Skills/help-getter/SKILL.md`.
